  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Lifesaving NFI, Tent and Protection Support to Earthquake-Affected Populations in T&#xFC;rkiye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the latest statement made by T&#xFC;rkiye&#x2019;s Disaster and Emergency Management Presidency (AFAD), as of 11 February 2023, a total of 20,665 individuals have lost their lives and 80,088 individuals were rescued after two major earthquakes and numerous aftershocks struck the region. These numbers are expected to increase further over the coming days/weeks due to prevailing cold weather conditions and the fact that some disaster zone areas have not yet been reached by search and rescue teams. In both affected and hosting areas, affected populations are in urgent need of Non-Food Items (NFI), including blankets, mattresses, and winter-resistant tents. Whilst local municipalities and AFAD are assessing infrastructures and residential buildings to ascertain their damages and safety levels, the need for more immediate shelter solutions will remain, as well as a need for winterization NFI assistance. This projects&#x2019; overall objective is to provide humanitarian assistance and protection services in T&#xFC;rkiye to save lives and respond to immediate humanitarian needs. The delivery of targeted lifesaving assistance is ensured through the procurement, transportation, and distribution of: (i) NFIs and (ii) winterization shelter support, as well as the (iii) provision of critical protection monitoring and support to earthquake-affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
